{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.domain`\n\nThe {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`habeas_sdk::domain::Domain` to define its node-identity type. Its\nerror type is introduced in {cite}`requirements.sdk.errors`:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    /// The *identifier* identifies a particular node in the graph.\n    type NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync;\n\n    // ... additional graph members ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.domain_types`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the requirement**\n- An application domain implements `habeas_sdk::domain::Domain`.\n- The domain is `Clone + Send + Sync`. This comes from the `Domain` declaration quoted in the requirement and in `requirements.sdk.domain`.\n- The associated type `NodeId` is `Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`.\n- The requirement lists no other bounds, so `NodeId` should be usable as an opaque identity.\n\n**Test coverage**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` is the main test.\n  - It defines a `Domain` implementation whose `NodeId` is an opaque `Identity(u8)`. That type derives only `Clone, PartialEq, Eq`, with no `Debug`, `Hash` or `Ord`. The test therefore fails to compile if the trait demands more than the required bounds.\n  - Its nested `check_bounds::<G: Domain>()` calls `identity::<G::NodeId>()`, where `identity<T: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync>`. It also calls `domain::<G>()`, which requires `Clone + Send + Sync`. If the trait loosened any required bound, this generic consumer would stop compiling.\n  - The test then uses the `NodeId` through `node_content`, `node_path`, `outgoing_edges`, and `load_evidence` / `store_evidence`. It asserts that identities are compared and distinguished: `assert_ne!` on node paths, and `Identity` successors compared with `==`, which relies on `Eq`.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[habeas_paths_preserve_opaque_segments_and_separate_all_node_kinds]` and `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` exercise the application's own `HabeasDomain` with its real node identity type. They show the application domain can implement `Domain` with its own `NodeId`. The tests in `src/authoring/sdk.rs` and `crates/trust-but-verify/tests` (the agent and criterion tests) also use domains whose `NodeId` is used generically.\n\n**Gaps**\nNo gap found. Each obligation is verified at compile time by the bound-check functions, and the behavioural assertions confirm that `NodeId` values work as clonable, comparable identities. The rest of `Domain` is delegated to other requirements: the error type to `requirements.sdk.errors`, and the other members to their own requirements. Those obligations need no test here.",
  "references": "cda4cd7719bca29bf0f608a354e6640e87eb395107be478cffddfaac97757bbf",
